  "query_preview": "..High pressure will sit over the Four Corners over\nthe next few days. This puts Arizona in a favorable spot for\nincreased moisture flow into the area which will lead to more\nwidespread shower and thunderstorm activity. With PWAT's hitting\n1.0-1.5\", storms will be able to put down more rain and as the\nsoil saturates throughout the week, flash flooding will definitely\nbe a concern. With the higher moisture and likely increased cloud\ncover, high temperatures will also drop below average for the\nfirst time in awhile.\n\nMoisture and POPs are expected to peak around Thursday. By Friday\na weak West Coast trough begins to move into the area which will\npush our high pressure center to the east, as well as introduce\nsome drier air across the region. By Saturday storm chances will\nbe confined mainly over the White Mountain region and the very\nhighest terrain. High temperatures will begin to recover back to\nmid August averages by Saturday or Sunday.",
